  "parameter_metadata": {},
  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "D-D fusion ignition achievable in dipole geometry at commercial scale (Q≥10, T_i ~100-200 keV, n ~10²¹ m⁻³, τ_E 20-40 s — extrapolations exceeding any validated MFE experiment)",
      "Superconducting coil path can replace the 700 MW copper coil draw with a cryogenic load of ~15 MW while preserving the PoloMac magnetic geometry",
      "Magnetic tunnel topology can physically support an in-vessel dipole coil through the plasma without compromising confinement",
      "Steady-state operation is achievable in the dipole geometry, avoiding pulsed-mode fatigue penalties",
      "Reduced field strength (2-3 T for D-T, vs 5.3 T tokamak baseline) is sufficient for fusion-relevant performance",
      "An in-vessel superconducting coil can survive fusion-relevant neutron fluence with radiation-hardened insulation"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "Tritium breeding blanket (Li blanket, FLiBe loop, breeding ratio management) — eliminated for D-D fuel cycle, saving ~$200-400M capital",
      "Lithium-6 enrichment infrastructure and supply chain (limited suppliers, environmentally sensitive)",
      "Beryllium neutron multiplier supply chain (sole-sourced from Materion)",
      "Tritium fuel procurement and on-site tritium plant — D-D uses deuterium at ~$5-10k/kg vs tritium at >$35,000/g",
      "Pulsed-operation thermal/mechanical fatigue costs vs pulsed tokamak designs (steady-state operation claimed)"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "In-vessel superconducting dipole coil with radiation-hardened insulation — no vendor currently supplies qualified radiation-hardened HTS coils",
      "Magnetic tunnel support structure passing through the plasma volume — novel mechanical concept with no precedent",
      "Enhanced remote handling for activated in-vessel coil removal/replacement through magnetic tunnel geometry (1.5× standard cost, drives forced outage rate)",
      "Oversized first wall, shield (~$804M), structure, and vacuum vessel driven by very large plasma volume (~4,000-8,000 m³, ~5× ITER) needed for adequate D-D fusion power",
      "Dedicated cryoplant (~$124M) sized for in-vessel SC coil cryogenic load in a high-radiation environment"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "700 MW copper-coil recirculating power penalty with no published superconducting coil design to resolve it; if SC cryo load exceeds ~100 MW, net power goes negative",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "No plasma confinement physics validation — MHD stability, confinement scaling, and transport coefficients are entirely unanalyzed; historical dipole experiments achieved only ~few eV / 10¹⁶ m⁻³, many orders of magnitude below fusion conditions",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "D-D ignition is unvalidated and ~142× more demanding than D-T by Lawson criterion; claimed Q≥10 at 100-200 keV is an extraordinary extrapolation with no experimental or physics-model support",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "No reactor design point published (Q, major radius, fusion power, thermal efficiency, net electric output all unknown), preventing any engineering-grade $/kWe estimate",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "In-vessel coil neutron shielding scheme, materials selection, and lifetime are unspecified; coil replacement through magnetic-tunnel geometry could drive capacity factor to 0.4-0.5 (LCOE penalty up to ~1.7×)",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Plant scale penalty: competitive D-D LCOE requires ~800-1000 MW fusion power and ~6,000-8,000 m³ plasma volume (larger than any fusion device ever built), partially or fully offsetting the blanket-elimination capital savings",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Commercial-scale plasma heating power and integration unspecified (only 5-10 kW ECH at 4 GHz prototype-scale defined); D-D requires heating systems many orders of magnitude more powerful",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Inconsistent field-strength claims in the primary source (\"3× weaker\" in abstract vs \"half magnetic field, i.e. 2-3 T rather than 5.3 T\" in §DT reactor conditions) are not reconciled by the paper",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "REBCO HTS supply chain scaling and radiation-hardened HTS insulation are unsolved problems shared with other in-vessel-coil concepts (cf. levitated-dipole, orbital-dipole)",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Independent assessment is limited to a C− tier rating from an unnamed \"fusion company tier list\"; no third-party plasma physics, system-code, or cost analysis exists",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ]
  },
